                  "DataSource": "Ian Daniells, Bill Manning and Luke Pearce (2002) Profile Descriptions. NSW Agriculture. Data processed by CSIRO for GRDC CSP00170 Measuring and managing soil water in Australian agriculture.",
                  "Comments": "Medium heavy clay - Profile MW52. Shrink and swell clay soil. Very deep soil (> 200 cm). Dispersive subsoil may limit penetration of water and reduce effective rooting depth. Slightly high ECe in subsoil is due to gypsum, not chloride. Strongly sodic subsoil. See Profile Descriptions publication for more details. DUL from nearby paddock. CLL field measured for wheat. No organic carbon available. Estimated at 1 % in surface layer. Adjust for local conditions. Salb estimated from texture instead of MunsellColour. For SWCON deeper layers with no Texture values were assumed to be same as the last layer with a Texture specified. Not georeferenced - located in nearest town/locality.",
